# `= =` with a space: one DS0110 with a fix to `==`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where a = = 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..23
  PIPELINE@0..22
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..22
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..22
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "a"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        EQ@17..18 "="
        WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
        EQ@19..20 "="
        WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
        LITERAL@21..22
          LONG@21..22 "1"
  WHITESPACE@22..23 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `= =` is not an operator
  --> query:1:18
  |
1 | from t | where a = = 1
  |                  ^^^ two `=` with a space between them
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `a == 1`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from t | where a == 1
which parses without errors
